# Managed by create-agentic-workspace. The block below is byte-identical to the shipped
# scripts/foundry-runtime.gitignore applier's own content (AC-BCL-5) so the two can never diverge.
# FOUNDRY-RUNTIME-GITIGNORE-BEGIN
# .foundry/ runtime partitions are ignored by default; the designed-tracked set is re-included.
/.foundry/*
!/.foundry/README.md
!/.foundry/build-provenance.yaml
!/.foundry/stack-profile.lock
# FOUNDRY-RUNTIME-GITIGNORE-END

# Local, UNGATED permission overrides — never commit them (PR #61 security review Risk 5).
# The floor model this workspace is scaffolded around distinguishes the committed
# .claude/settings.json, whose `allow` rules take effect only after the operator accepts the trust
# dialog that lists them, from .claude/settings.local.json, which is read with NO trust ceremony
# (it is where the harness's "always allow" persist option writes). A committed settings.local.json
# would therefore propagate ungated local grants to every clone, with no dialog and no review —
# which is precisely the shadowing that /foundry:doctor's permission-floor probe exists to report.
/.claude/settings.local.json
